From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pw4-port <pw4-port@localhost>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:59:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] PW4 Android: keep the stock run voltage of VDD_ARM/VDD_SOC at
 probe

The DVS init wrote 1.1 V while the CPU was already at 996 MHz from the
stock kernel; cpufreq saw no change and left it there until the first
transition (35-90 s). Keep a higher run voltage already in the PMIC.
---
 drivers/regulator/bd71827-regulator.c | 14 +++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/regulator/bd71827-regulator.c b/drivers/regulator/bd71827-regulator.c
index d2377f91..99f8fb0a 100755
--- a/drivers/regulator/bd71827-regulator.c
+++ b/drivers/regulator/bd71827-regulator.c
@@ -664,7 +664,19 @@ static int bd71827_buck12_dvs_init(struct bd71827_pmic *pmic)
 		reg_susp = BD71827_REG_BUCK1_VOLT_SUSP + i*0x2;
 		dev_info(pmic->dev, "Buck%d: DVS Run-Idle-Susp[%d - %d - %d].\n", i, buck_dvs->voltage[0], buck_dvs->voltage[1], buck_dvs->voltage[2]);
 		selector = regulator_map_voltage_iterate(pmic->rdev[i], buck_dvs->voltage[0], buck_dvs->voltage[0]);
-		if(selector < 0) {
+		/*
+		 * PW4 Android: the kernel takes over from the stock one with the
+		 * CPU already at 996 MHz and VDD_ARM/VDD_SOC at 1.275 V. cpufreq
+		 * sees no frequency change, so lowering the run voltage here would
+		 * leave the CPU at 996 MHz on 1.1 V until the first transition.
+		 * Keep a higher run voltage.
+		 */
+		ret = bd71827_reg_read(bd71827, reg_run);
+		if (selector >= 0 && ret >= 0 && (ret & BUCK1_RUN_MASK) > selector) {
+			dev_info(pmic->dev, "Buck%d: keep run selector %#x (above %#x)\n",
+				 i, ret & BUCK1_RUN_MASK, selector);
+			selector = -1;
+		} else if(selector < 0) {
 			dev_err(pmic->dev, "%s(): not found selector for Run voltage [%d]\n", __func__, buck_dvs->voltage[0]);
 		} else {
 			val = (selector & BUCK1_RUN_MASK);
-- 
